<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - Dutch April output seen up 5.8 pct y/y.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Dutch April output seen up 5.8 pct y/y.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists expect manufacturing production figures for April, due tomorrow, to show a bigger year-on-year increase than in March.</p>
<p>The month-on-month figure for April is expected to drop.</p>
<p>&quot;A favourable outlook and high sales in April could result in a stronger growth year-on-year than in the previous month,&quot; said one economist.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT--Date-Period-Indicator------------Consensus--Range------Pvs</p>
<p> 0730 12/6 April  Manufac. output M/M  -0.5 pct   -2.3/0.0   3.7</p>
<p> 0730 12/6 April  Manufac. output Y/Y   5.8 pct    4.0/6.5   5.1</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING, MeesPierson, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
